The residual autocorrelation is much smaller but still present (@fig-ex41-arx-acf). The coefficient of $x$ (-4.506) is closer to $-4$, but it only measures the immediate effect of $x$, since $y_{t-1}$ carries part of the past effect of $x$. If $x$ increased by one unit permanently, the long-run effect would be $\hat{\beta}_1/(1-\hat{\phi}) = -10.21$, which is far from the true $-4$. Thus, the ARMAX model is misspecified. The data were generated with AR(1) errors, which also require the term $-\phi\beta_1 x_{t-1}$.


